   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. I did not run it through a parser, so the stereo marks and the fatty-chain length are the least certain parts.\n\n**Macrocycle (disulfide-bridged):**\n- N-terminal acetyl on a penicillamine (Pen), then Asn, Thr and 7-methyl-Trp.\n- Next come Lys(N-acetyl) and a second Pen.\n- The two Pen side chains are joined by the S\u2013S bond.\n\n**Chain leaving the ring, in order from the second Pen:**\n1. Tyr with an O-CH2CH2NH2 ether.\n2. 2-Naphthylalanine.\n3. 4-Aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid (a spiro ring).\n4. Lys whose side-chain NH carries a succinyl group, which is linked to a trimethylammonium \u03b2-amino acid, NH-CH(CH2COOH)CH2N\u207a(CH3)3.\n5. Asn.\n6. 3-Pyridylalanine.\n7. N-methylglycine (sarcosine).\n8. Orn with a C-terminal primary amide.\n\n**Orn side chain:** two repeats of C(=O)CH2O(CH2)2O(CH2)2NH, then C(=O)CH2CH2 into \u03b3-Glu. The \u03b3-Glu \u03b1-nitrogen carries the fatty acid.\n\n**Fatty acid:** I counted 18 carbons in total (C(=O), 16 CH2 and the terminal COOH), an octadecanedioic acid. This is estimated from the drawn chain length.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I assigned @/@@ from the wedges and hashes as I read them; some of these are my best judgement.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2cc3cccc(C)c3[nH]2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(OCCN)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc3ccccc3c2)C(=O)NC2(CCOCC2)C(=O)N[C@H](CCCCNC(=O)CCC(=O)N[C@H](CC(O)=O)C[N+](C)(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2cccnc2)C(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N[C@H](CCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC(O)=O)C(O)=O)C(N)=O)C(C)(C)SSC1(C)C"
